---
title: "No more price emails - The Zero Fog"
permalink: /no-thanks/
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{# The landing side of E13's P.P.S.: "one click here and I stop." The click carries the join
   token; the page calls wr-preferences, which sets no_sales on the registration, and wr-notify
   keeps the promise at send time. This is deliberately NOT an unsubscribe - the person stays on
   the list and keeps every non-sales email. #}

{% block head_extras %}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
{% endblock %}

{% block page_css %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/pages/replay-3.css' | v }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<a href="/" class="brand">The Zero Fog</a>
<button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" onclick="toggleTheme()">Light</button>

<div class="replay">

  <div id="ntWorking">
    <h1>One second...</h1>
  </div>

  <div id="ntDone" hidden>
    <h1>Done. Nothing more about the price.</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">The useful emails still come. And if you ever do want the protocol,
    the door stays open at <a href="/sales/">thezerofog.com/sales</a> - you just won't hear
    about it from me again.</p>
  </div>

  <div id="ntNoToken" hidden>
    <h1>This link is missing its code.</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Please use the link from your email - it carries the code that tells us
    whose emails to change. Nothing has been changed yet.</p>
  </div>

  <div id="ntError" hidden>
    <h1>That didn't go through.</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Nothing has been changed. Try the link from your email once more, or
    just reply to any email with "no price emails" and I'll set it by hand.</p>
  </div>

</div>

{% endblock %}

{% block page_scripts %}
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/pages/no-thanks.js' | v }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
